title: Linux Injection via /proc/pid/mem
id: eac35e08-0dce-4909-8201-6a0045006f43
status: experimental
description: Detects writing to another process's memory through /proc/<pid>/mem or /proc/<pid>/maps, a Linux code-injection technique that modifies a running process without ptrace.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1055/009/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '/proc/'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '/mem'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'dd '
      - '>'
      - 'write'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
falsepositives:
  - Debugging and diagnostics
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1055.009
